FEATURE: auto-writer-docs
DATE: 2026-08-26
SCOPE: guide and runnable example for AutoWriter, plus one API coherence fix
FOLLOWS: changelog/auto-writer-fixes

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AFFECTED PROJECTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

vUX library (this repository) — the only project affected.

  - doc/auto-writer.md              new guide
  - doc/README.md                   guide listed, example listed, pending list trimmed
  - examples/autowriter/            new runnable example (index.html, main.js, README.md)
  - vUX-autoWriter.js               deleteText() target resolution

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

AutoWriter was the last module carrying neither a guide nor an example, having been
repaired under feature 'auto-writer-fixes' with nothing to show the repaired behaviour.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT CHANGED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The guide covers the mechanism, the directive syntax, collection mode, erasing, the
cursor's three states, the write-only config table, cancellation, the validation errors,
and three recipes. It leads with the two ways this component departs from the house
pattern: there is no initialize(), and the component owns the inside of the element it
is given.

The example is designed rather than plain, which is a deliberate departure from the other
example pages in this repository. Those are utilitarian because they demonstrate
structural behaviour; this component's whole output is a visual effect, so the page is
built to show it — a typed hero, a live playground over every config property, isolated
directive demos, collection mode, and a section whose five buttons all throw.

One code change came out of writing it. deleteText() erased from the element it was
given, while writeText() types into a span INSIDE that element, so passing the same
element to both — the obvious reading, and what the example does — removed the caret
before it removed any text. deleteText() now resolves to the written span when there is
one, and still erases arbitrary elements directly when there is not.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PUBLIC API
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Unchanged. deleteText()'s signature and its behaviour on elements this component never
wrote to are the same; only its behaviour on a target holding a '.vAutoWriter' span
changes, and there it moves from wrong to right.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STILL OUTSTANDING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  - src/helpers.js validateInteger() returns a boolean instead of throwing, disabling
    that check in this module and in $$.randomInteger. Carried over from
    'auto-writer-fixes'; still wants its own feature entry.
  - Nine modules remain undocumented: Carousel, FormValidator, ListScroller,
    TouchHandler, ToolTip, Resizer, TimeLineList, CShapes, DOMDrawer.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
VERIFICATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Every string the example types was executed against the real module in the Node harness
(30 assertions), which caught one cosmetic defect in a preset before it shipped. The
module's own suite grew to 29 assertions with the deleteText target change. All example
selectors were cross-checked against the markup, and every asset the page requests
returns 200 when the repository root is served over HTTP. The page itself was not opened
in a browser — there is none in this environment — so its visual result is unconfirmed.
